# Every PR needs a human reviewer; these paths need a specific one.
#
# A file matched by no rule below still needs the branch protection review —
# CODEOWNERS adds a named reviewer, it does not replace the requirement.
#
# Two owners on every line, never one. A sole owner who is also the author
# cannot be reviewed at all: GitHub refuses self-approval, so the code-owner
# rule blocks forever instead of ever being satisfied.
#
# `@samouraiworld/reviewers` widens that beyond two: any member of the team
# satisfies the rule, so the approver pool grows by a team membership change
# rather than by a pull request in every repository.
#
# A name here only counts if it holds write access on this repository. Without
# it GitHub ignores the entry silently -- no error on the pull request, no
# failing check, the review simply never counts, and the file reads as a wider
# pool than it is. `gh api repos/samouraiworld/<repo>/codeowners/errors` is what
# reports it; a green pull request does not.

*                       @zxxma @louis14448 @samouraiworld/reviewers

